[issue.1521]
number = 1521
title = "[Coherence] The blanket glob override hands glob 14 to rimraf 2 and globby 6, which call glob as a callback function, so the next-pwa clean step in `next build` breaks"
revision = "210639d0360c53f5c2fdd81c9c7c5e84b24b8c84"
verdict = "task"
evidence = "Commit fc3d178f2a01ba91683a726d3468dbd68f3cf8dc remains the latest change to these dependencies: apps/perps/package.json:105 and :145 force glob 14.0.2, apps/perps/pnpm-lock.yaml:12202, :10981, :11192, :11695 and :12841 retain next-pwa -> clean-webpack-plugin -> del 4 -> globby 6/rimraf 2 with that glob, apps/perps/package-lock.json:11422, :12772 and :15938 confirm the npm resolution, and apps/perps/next.config.js:1 loads the incompatible chain before its development-disable option at :3 can apply."
close_comment = "The PWA cleanup dependency chain still resolves a non-callable glob export into globby 6, which fails while loading the build configuration; glob 14 retains sync, so the failure occurs before the cleanup hook runs. A follow-up task upgrades the cleanup dependency without lowering the security floors and adds a regression test for the production cleanup path."

